  "question": {
    "text": "A wire suspended vertically from one of its ends is stretched by attaching a weight of $200 \\mathrm{~N}$ to the lower end. The weight stretches the wire by $1 \\mathrm{~mm}$. Then the elastic energy stored in the wire is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$0.2 \\mathrm{~J}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$10 \\mathrm{~J}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$20 \\mathrm{~J}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$0.1 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Elastic energy $=\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\mathrm{F} \\times \\mathrm{x}$\n$$\n\\mathrm{F}=200 \\mathrm{~N}, \\mathrm{x}=1 \\mathrm{~mm}=10^{-3} \\mathrm{~m} \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{E}=\\frac{1}{2} \\times 200 \\times 1 \\times 10^{-3}=0.1 \\mathrm{~J}\n$$"
  }
}